/// BACKEND DECLINE — "parameter reference has no local slot" (2026-07-15, seed rcdzc, iter 47). `cdz check`
/// is CLEAN (type-level fine); `cdz compile -t wasm` DECLINES at emit with "parameter reference has no
/// local slot" — a slot-allocation gap in the backend, not a type error.
///
/// Hit organically building a type-checker (`tycheck`): the `If` typing rule factored into a mutually-
/// recursive helper `check-if` (↔ `check`) that gates a nested recursive check on `if teq(ct, TBool)`.
///
/// SHARP — ALL THREE jointly required (drop any one and it COMPILES):
///   1. MUTUAL recursion: `check ↔ helper` (helper calls check, check calls helper). INLINING the helper
///      body into `check` (making it self-recursive) COMPILES.
///   2. the `if` CONDITION is a FUNCTION CALL on a match-bound sum payload — `if is-bool(ct) then …`,
///      where `ct` was bound by `match check(c) { Ok(ct) => … }`. Replacing the call with an INLINE match
///      (`if (match ct { TBool => true | TInt => false }) then …`) COMPILES.
///   3. the then-branch does a NESTED `match` on ANOTHER recursive call returning a heap SUM
///      (`match check(t) { Ok(tt) => … }`), and the whole thing returns a `Result` (heap sum).
/// (An Int64-only analogue of the same shape COMPILES — the heap-sum payloads matter.)
///
/// So: a match-bound sum payload passed to a CALL forming an `if` condition, in a MUTUALLY-recursive
/// function whose branch nests another recursive heap-sum match, gets a `Core::Param`/`LocalRef` with no
/// wasm local slot assigned at emit. Likely the same slot-allocation family as the earlier slot-alias /
/// disjoint-scratch bugs (`select.rs`): the call-in-if-condition + mutual-call arg layout hands a
/// parameter reference a slot the emit never reserved. Fix locus: backend/wasm/select.rs slot allocation.
///
/// `main` exercises the `If` path so `cdz compile <this>` reproduces. WORKAROUND: inline the helper
/// (self-recursive), OR make the `if` condition an inline `match` rather than a call (both compile) —
/// `tycheck` cannot do either cleanly without losing the factoring, so it is WITHHELD from `src/`.
type Ty =
  | TInt
  | TBool

type TErr =
  | CondNotBool

type Exp =
  | Num(Int64)
  | If(Exp, Exp)

def is-bool(t: Ty) = match t with
  | TBool => true
  | TInt => false

def check(e: Exp) = match e with
  | Exp.Num(_) => Result.Ok(TInt)
  | Exp.If(c, t) => check-if(c, t)

/// The mutually-recursive helper: `if is-bool(ct)` (a CALL condition on the match-bound payload `ct`)
/// gating a nested recursive `match check(t)`. This is the shape that declines "no local slot".
def check-if(c: Exp, t: Exp) = match check(c) with
  | Result.Ok(ct) =>
    (if is-bool(ct) then
      (match check(t) with
        | Result.Ok(tt) => Result.Ok(tt)
        | Result.Err(et) => Result.Err(et))
    else
      Result.Err(CondNotBool))
  | Result.Err(ec) => Result.Err(ec)

/// `if 1 then 2` — an ill-formed If (cond is Int, not Bool) exercises the `If` path; the point is that
/// `cdz compile` declines "no local slot" REGARDLESS of the value.
def main() = match check(Exp.If(Exp.Num(1), Exp.Num(2))) with
  | Result.Ok(_) => 1
  | Result.Err(_) => 0

export { main }

/// RESOLVED 2026-07-15 (trunk@9ae29c12a, fix f15414e7 — recovered from a silent drop by pr-sync): the backend "parameter reference has no local slot" decline for a mutual-recursive helper gating an if cond is fixed; repro compiles + checks clean.
